BDOSXM (probes/disk/bdosxm.asm), 2026-11-17: the console-output matrix. Raw captures: scratchpad/XM_stock.out
(the CF-3300) and scratchpad/XM_ours.out (zerobas); the capture block is the mark, LINLEN, the entry column, then
4 bytes per case: ($F237) [the count], CSRX, CSRY, and the A the last BDOS call returned.
Before EVERY case: CONOUT 'x' 'x' (completes any pending escape / prefix), CR, ESC 'Y' 32+10 32+20 -- the cursor to
CSRY 11, CSRX 21 while the count is 3 on the CF-3300 (Y, r, c counted; the ESC not). zerobas's setup leaves the
count at 4 (it counts the ESC: D-CONCOL), so its counts are offset; read the CF-3300 column for the rule.
⚠️ SKIPPED CASES (511: DIRIO v=$FF, 548: STROUT v='$'): no BDOS output call is made, so the A recorded there is the
PROBE'S OWN register (the value it compared, $FF / $24), NOT a BDOS result; count / CSRX / CSRY are the bare setup's.
Modes: 0 CONOUT v; 1 DIRIO-out v (v=$FF skipped: DIRIO input); 2 STROUT v,'$' (v='$' skipped); 3 CONOUT ESC then
CONOUT v; 4 CONOUT 1 (graphic prefix) then CONOUT v. Extras X0..X6 at the end. Case number = mode*256 + v.
head: LINLEN CF 29 zb 29; the count at program entry CF 0 zb 0

